// A `@viewable` contract must be able to grant something. The mark is spent by an implementation whose
// return type is a `type view`, so a member can only ever mint if it returns a view or a contract a view
// may implement. Here no member does, so the mark is INERT — and an inert grant is how the whole model
// fails silently: the author believes minting is permitted where it is not.
@viewable type contract Sized for resource { fn int32 size(); fn bool isEmpty(); }

type resource Bag implements Sized {
    int32 n;
    public ctor of(int32 n) { this.n = n; }
    public fn int32 size() { return this.n; }
    public fn bool isEmpty() { return this.n == 0; }
}
fn int32 main() { return 0; }
